<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">woodwork</ansi> (skill)

Woodwork is the craft of turning logs and timber into weapons, shields,
bows and arrows, furniture, fittings and tool hafts. It is governed by
<ansi fg="yellow">Dexterity</ansi>, since joinery and shaping reward a steady, precise hand.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">woodworking bench</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             Look for one in the Craftsmen's Quarter (West) in Thornwall,
             the Cooperage Floor in New Plymouth, the Cooperage at the
             Confluence, the Woodworker's House in Amber Valley, the Timber
             Yard at Kilnreach, the Lumber Camp on Cascade Pass Road, the
             Woodcutter's Camp on the North Road, and the Fletcher's Ledge in
             Pothole Coulee. You can also build your own for your lodging.
  Materials: Logs you fell yourself (<ansi fg="command">help chop</ansi>) or buy, sawn into lumber.
  Tools:     A saw for planks, boards and shafts, an axe to split staves, a
             carving knife for bows and arrows (<ansi fg="command">help tools</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Recipes ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Lumber</ansi>      <ansi fg="command">saw-planks</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">saw-boards</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">split-staves</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">cut-shafts</ansi>,
              <ansi fg="command">whittle-shafts</ansi> (from branches, anywhere),
              <ansi fg="command">ironwood-haft</ansi> (for masterwork tools)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Bows</ansi>        <ansi fg="command">self-bow</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">hunting-bow</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">longbow</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">horn-bow</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ammunition</ansi>  <ansi fg="command">fletch-arrows</ansi> (anywhere), <ansi fg="command">make-bolts</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow">Arms</ansi>        <ansi fg="command">wooden-club</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">quarterstaff</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">wooden-shield</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">kite-shield</ansi>
  <ansi fg="yellow">Furniture</ansi>   <ansi fg="command">wooden-chest</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">bed-frame</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">woodworking-bench</ansi>

Furniture goes home with you: <ansi fg="command">use</ansi> a chest, bed frame or workbench inside your
own lodging to set it up, the same as a deed from the letting agent.

Bowstrings come from tailoring (sinew or horsehair), glue from cooking (bone),
horn from butchering, feathers from birds, and arrowheads from a smith or a
jeweler (iron or bone). The grade of your lumber, and of your tools, carries
into what you make.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Woods ━━━</ansi>

Staves and shafts remember the wood they were cut from, and so do the bows
and arrows made from them: a longbow (yew), a quiver of arrows (cedar).

  Bows       <ansi fg="yellow">ash</ansi>      quick to draw (+8% speed) and light
             <ansi fg="yellow">elm</ansi>      steady (+5% accuracy), a little heavy
             <ansi fg="yellow">yew</ansi>      the best: +6% speed, +6% accuracy, lighter
  Arrows     <ansi fg="yellow">cedar</ansi>    +6% accuracy      <ansi fg="yellow">spruce</ansi>   +4% accuracy
             <ansi fg="yellow">juniper</ansi>  +5% damage, tough <ansi fg="yellow">larch</ansi>    +4% damage, +2% accuracy
             <ansi fg="yellow">birch</ansi>    +3% damage, tough <ansi fg="yellow">cypress</ansi>  +3% accuracy, tougher
             <ansi fg="yellow">willow</ansi>   toughest, -3% accuracy
             <ansi fg="yellow">alder</ansi>, <ansi fg="yellow">pine</ansi>  plain and cheap

A tough arrow is often picked up whole after a shot instead of being used
up. You cannot choose which staves or shafts a recipe takes, so carry only
the wood you want to work. Yew needs an iron axe to fell.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Woodwork improves through use. Each completed craft attempt (success or
failure) has a chance to advance the skill.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including woodwork ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting a woodwork recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current woodwork skill level.

